<title>USA: Delta sees moderate yield decline in June.</title>
<headline>Delta sees moderate yield decline in June.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA, Ga. 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delta Air Lines said Thursday it saw a moderate year-over-year system yield decline in June driven primarily by weaker domestic yields.</p>
<p>The carrier said the continued weakness in domestic yields reflects the reimposition of the 10 percent domestic passenger ticket tax and increases in lower-yielding domestic leisure demand.</p>
<p>Delta reported a June load factor of 77.77 percent compared to 76.59 percent.</p>
</text>
